{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2521","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2521","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2521\",\"parent_revision\":\"f4bd082cf9737bc9fd4398fe15d534e8ad1a5c535cd3827ebceff56d75b9a992\",\"root_revision\":\"f4bd082cf9737bc9fd4398fe15d534e8ad1a5c535cd3827ebceff56d75b9a992\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe development harness has multiple MCP interfaces that return structured data (sam_plan read, sam_plan ready, backlog_view entries, artifact reads). There is no platform-level contract defining how these interfaces must handle per-request token limits for AI agent consumption. Each tool either has no pagination at all (sam_plan read/ready) or a partial solution that still overflows on large data (backlog_view section filter overflowed at 112K chars even when filtering by section name during #2515 session work). AI agents working within token-limited contexts cannot reliably map (what does this data contain?), navigate (give me a bounded portion), or extract (give me this specific item) from MCP data-returning interfaces without risking context overflow. Tool-by-tool fixes applied ad-hoc produce inconsistent interfaces and repeat the same design work for every new tool.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: the contract should define a standard three-layer progressive disclosure pattern \u2014 map (TOC view of structure and contents), navigate (page-based access with current page and pages remaining), extract (item-by-ID access). This pattern should apply consistently to all existing and future MCP tools that return structured data. #2515 is planned as the first implementation of this contract on sam_plan read/ready.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: MCP progressive disclosure contract for all data-returning interfaces\\nDate: 2026-05-31\\nGoal: Define and implement a platform-level progressive disclosure contract (map/navigate/extract) with backlog_view reference implementation, unblocking #2515.\\n\\n**Decision: APPROVED**\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|-----------|--------|---------|\\n| 1 | Reference design studied (mdsel-mcp) | AVAILABLE | `.tmp/scratch/reports/mdsel-mcp-study.md` \u2014 parameter-presence routing, ordinal dot-path selectors, head/tail bounded extraction, graceful truncation documented |\\n| 2 | Pagination layer: MCP only vs backend protocol | AVAILABLE | tool-inventory confirmed 0 backend protocol changes required; all 8 tools can be handled at MCP response layer only |\\n| 3 | Full inventory of in-scope MCP tools | AVAILABLE | `.tmp/scratch/reports/mcp-tool-inventory.md` \u2014 43 tools, 8 need pagination, 1 canonical backend method (not 36 files) |\\n| 4 | Entry-level bounding mechanism | AVAILABLE | User decision: path-based ordinal dot-notation (mdsel/markdown-parser-py native). Flat map, no indentation. Ordinal IS the navigate selector. |\\n| 5 | progressive_markdown/ concerns diagnosed | AVAILABLE | `.tmp/scratch/reports/progressive-markdown-analysis.md` \u2014 4 concerns with exact file paths, line numbers, fix plans. Implementation work (not a planning prerequisite). |\\n| 6 | Contract document | DERIVABLE | Will be produced during implementation (it IS the deliverable). Discovery artifact defines the full spec. |\\n| 7 | Testable acceptance criteria | AVAILABLE | 11 testable ACs in discovery artifact, grounded in real fixture content from #2515 (51 sections, 112K chars), #2521, #996, #1857. |\\n| 8 | #2515 sequencing | AVAILABLE | User decision: contract + backlog_view reference implementation both required before #2515 proceeds. |\\n\\n**DERIVABLE assumptions to carry forward:**\\n- Ordinal path construction for nested headings (flat `sections_index` vs nested body) is a design question for the architect \u2014 does not block planning\\n- `head=N` tokenisation unit (tiktoken vs char-with-factor) is an architect decision \u2014 does not block planning\\n- Silent-fallback fix backward-compat: caller migration path is an architect concern \u2014 does not block planning\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **feat: mcp progressive disclosure contract for all data-returning interfaces** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 #2515 implementation, 2026-05-31\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-31\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-06-01)\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\nPre-existing concerns in progressive_markdown/ surfaced during 2026-05-31 code review \u2014 must be addressed as part of implementing the progressive disclosure contract:\\n\\n1. **ProgressiveDisclosure vs MarkdownNavigator unified output** \u2014 two systems with divergent output contracts (dict with next_call hint vs Pydantic NavigationResult with no hint). Architecture decision: both should return NavigationResult; ProgressiveDisclosure's raw dict return is the mistake. Unification belongs in the plan for this item, not ad-hoc.\\n\\n2. **AmbiguousSectionRefError never raised** \u2014 resolve_section() silently returns first match on slug collision; docstrings and public API surface advertise the exception as raised. Either raise it or remove it from the API surface.\\n\\n3. **MarkdownIndexer.build() monolith** \u2014 150 lines, 74 statements, 40 locals (PLR0915/PLR0914). Needs decomposition into _process_heading_token(), _process_fence_token(), _finalise_sections(), _BuildState dataclass.\\n\\n4. **__init__.py docstring stale** \u2014 still shows qualified import path after chunk_text/paginate_results were added to package-level __all__.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:14a1aaea8ff101f14c5e0abf35e0d4a5 -->\\n\",\"digest\":\"d3f5a0c7adef2bee76351246b5d4acc0b3d80b0d0a692335cd7ce7cd5a352bbd\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCNnew\"}"}